      {
        "text": "Real (chained-dollar) goods PCE decreased 0.4 percent in April while services increased 0.1 percent, showing the goods component did not rise in quantity terms. However, these are chained-dollar measures, not current-dollar measures, so they do not directly refute the claim about current-dollar values; they only show the claim's implied quantity logic fails and that the aggregate increase could have been driven by prices or by services.",
